  "48": {
    "title": "Technology Procurement Framework — AI",
    "text": "Slide 48 — Technology Procurement Framework — AI\nSession 4 Emerging Technology & AI\nApplying the Framework to AI\nAI demand can grow quickly because both usage and unit economics are variable.\n\nDemand Management — Cost Management\nMake AI demand visible and attributable:\n• Inventory use cases, users, models and workload owners.\n• Track token, request, compute and storage consumption.\n• Set quotas, approval thresholds, budgets and alerts.\n• Allocate cost through team-level showback or chargeback.\nToolkit: usage telemetry; quotas; approval thresholds; budgets/alerts; showback/chargeback.\n\nDemand Management — Cost Optimization\nUse the least-cost approach that still works:\n• Match the model to task complexity.\n• Shorten prompts and trim unnecessary context.\n• Cache repeated outputs and batch/reuse requests where appropriate.\n• Remove unnecessary calls before scaling the workflow.\nToolkit: model-to-task routing; prompt/context control; caching; batching; call elimination.\n\nCommercial Negotiation — Commercial Levers\nProtect economics as AI usage evolves:\n• Negotiate token / unit pricing and volume tiers.\n• Challenge committed spend and preserve flexibility between models.\n• Cover future models, support and professional services.\n• Protect data use, ownership, IP position, portability and exit rights.\nToolkit: unit rates; commitments; future-model terms; data / IP; exit rights.\n\nDo not negotiate large AI commitments against an immature use-case and consumption forecast.",
    "topicIds": [
      "TOPIC_27",
      "TOPIC_03",
      "TOPIC_16"
    ]
  },
