  "57": {
    "title": "Software Maintenance and Support",
    "text": "ITPF — Slide 57 — Software Maintenance and Support\nSession 3 Cloud Computing\nSoftware Maintenance and Support\nTypes of software maintenance and support. Digitalization Paradox.\nOverview\nExercise\nMaintenance\n1\nCorrective maintenance\nRectify an actual fault\n2\nPerfective maintenance\nImprove the value\n3\nAdaptive maintenance\nMaintain compliance\n4\nPreventative maintenance\nPrevent a future fault\nSupport\n1\nCustomer Support\nAct as Single Point of Contact for all tickets\nAssist end users on daily operations\nAddress Application usage requests\nProvide End User training\nScheduled Job Management\nProvide issue analysis to L2 if unable to resolve\nProvide ticket updates to end users\nCoordinate with L2 on open issues\n2\nBusiness Process Support\nEnsure application availability to end users\nEnsure business continuity\nResolve usage queries\nConfiguration Support\nAdmin – User management\nManage workflows, roles, minor label changes etc.\nmanage minor enhancements\nResolve Integration failures\nPatch updates for data correction\nTesting of any developments\nProvide Training to L1\nCoordinate with L3 & L4 team\n3\nTechnical Support\nChange Requests related to new functionality development or integration developments where the effort is upto 3 man-days\nBug Fixes\nDeep Configurations\nTemporary Fixes\nEnhancement Tag Deliveries\n4\nProduct Support\n(Part of Subscription)\nStandard Product Support\nPatch updates\nVersion Upgrades\nChange Request where code level changes are required\nWhich two types of maintenance are normally included in the SaaS fee?\n1\nCorrective maintenance\nRectify an actual fault\n2\nPerfective maintenance\nImprove the value\n3\nAdaptive maintenance\nMaintain compliance\n4\nPreventative maintenance\nPrevent a future fault\nSelect exactly two tiles.\n©",
    "topicIds": [
      "TOPIC_09",
      "TOPIC_10"
    ]
  },
  "58": {
    "title": "Essential Cloud TCO Elements",
    "text": "Essential Cloud TCO Elements\nSession 3 Cloud Computing\n\nThe slide maps the main cost components that need to be considered when comparing cloud sourcing options and calculating total cost of ownership.\n\nCloud deployment:\n- Public cloud\n- Private cloud\n\nCloud service:\n- SaaS\n- PaaS\n- IaaS\n\nInfrastructure and hosting cost elements:\n- Middleware and operating system cost\n- Hosting fee\n- Additional environment/location costs such as disaster recovery and sandbox\n\nSoftware applications:\n- Commercial off-the-shelf (COTS)\n- Custom software\n- Software rental fee\n\nSoftware deployment:\n- Customisation and deployment\n- Internal deployment\n- Onshore/offshore deployment cost\n\nSupport and maintenance:\n- External support and maintenance\n- Internal support\n- Internal IT cost\n\nTeaching point:\nCloud TCO is broader than the cloud service fee. The sourcing model, software model, deployment approach, supporting environments, implementation resources and ongoing support all create cost. Buyers should compare the complete cost architecture rather than comparing hosting or subscription price alone.",
    "topicIds": [
      "TOPIC_09",
      "TOPIC_10"
    ]
  },
